WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.770
It's Tuesday, November 10, and this is the Transhuman Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.990
Here are the last 24 hours in transhumanism, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.840
Fast forward.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:21.920
Anthropic says a thousand of its AI agents machine-checked Fermat's Last Theorem in 30 hours.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:28.090
In an early trial, one gene-editing infusion cut a risky blood fat by 63%.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.890
The same model, Anthropic says,

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:38.110
built a working operating system from an empty folder in 8 days.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:41.160
Meanwhile, Meta released Muse Ember,

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.540
a cheap little model built for the busywork AI agents repeat all day.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.090
In early tests,

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:52.720
a comfier brain-reading cap from China held 94% typing accuracy all day.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.190
In a small study,

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:59.510
an AI reading ER patients' words flagged all 30 who later developed PTSD.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:00.700
Back home,

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:06.630
Sydney researchers tied under four huff-and-puff minutes a day to 48% less dementia.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.480
And in Hong Kong health records,

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:13.860
people on common bone-strengthening drugs had up to 24% less dementia.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.970
In Germany, teens most stressed by lockdowns showed faster-ticking DNA ageing clocks.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:22.660
Kids and adults didn't.

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:25.780
And in mice, the heart doesn't age evenly.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:29.320
Inflammation and scarring cluster around the valves.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.980
On to wellbeing.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:36.530
Compass has asked the FDA to approve its psilocybin therapy for hard-to-treat depression.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.280
And in a year-long trial,

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:44.250
Lilly's daily weight-loss pill cut sleep apnea severity by up to 44%.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.650
Now, the catch. After nine tumours,

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:52.490
the FDA is probing Zolgensma, a one-time gene therapy for kids.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.020
And links can mislead. In a huge study,

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:59.670
long-feared bladder drugs looked no worse for dementia than newer ones.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.240
Over in robotics, Boston Dynamics bolted scooter wheels onto Atlas.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.910
It learned to skate in simulation first.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:13.890
And in orbit, a Caltech robot assembled part of an antenna on its own,

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:15.170
a first in space.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:16.110
Oh,

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:21.810
and China's space station chilled atoms to about ten trillionths of a degree above absolute zero.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:24.920
So yes, life's on fast forward.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:28.690
Just keep watching the whole tape, not only the highlights.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.510
Zoom out, and the line only goes up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.710
Somehow, the future keeps landing early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.350
That's one day of news. Imagine what a year looks like.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.170
You've been watching the Transhuman Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.330
Stay well. Same time tomorrow?

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
